  "body": "Consolidates existing fan-club and event-moment engagement into a capability-gated interaction layer shared by web and native clients. Publications gain catalog-backed reactions, transactional counts, cursor-paginated discussions, replies with tombstones, stable mentions, owner comment policies, scoped moderation, bilateral blocking, notification preferences and exact discussion links. Existing legacy engagement and references are preserved; converted writers delegate to the canonical model.\n\nThe enabled publication kinds are club posts/memories, events/moments, recordings/sessions, record releases, artist releases, classifieds and directory profiles. Imported artist social-sync records remain disabled until they have explicit publication authority. Entity-specific visibility and current ownership/management permissions compose with interaction authorization; historical creator metadata grants no catalog management authority. Owners can hide/restore comments on their publications but cannot exercise administrator removal or report decisions.\n\nWeb and native components share server semantics, progressive disclosure and shallow visual indentation. Deep links load exact comment context and preserve accessible focus. Publication links select the referenced item even on later catalog pages or another club tab. Subsequent collection refreshes preserve manual pagination, including when new publications shift the linked item\u2019s index; a failing-before/passing-after regression covers this behavior. Notification delivery respects privacy/preferences and aggregates reactions. Audited moderation notices reach affected authors across social blocks without revealing private publication content or granting access. Plain text preserves Unicode/mention offsets; canonical create/edit rejects whitespace-only bodies. All five moderation actions require bounded, nonblank JSON string reasons; rejected input leaves state and evidence unchanged. Server checks cover idempotency, concurrency, revisions, input validation, rate limits and permissions.\n\nThe release manifest has **155 entries**: the production baseline 115, eight compatibility prerequisites and 32 interaction migrations. Registered SQL remains byte-for-byte immutable. Activation atomically validates/converts legacy engagement, preserves stable aliases and permanently fences legacy writers. Missing legacy authors refuse activation. After activation, emergency pause waits for admitted writes/delivery through shared runtime admission locks, then fences new writes while retaining authorized reads. Existing targets are read without registration writes; absent targets stay unregistered during pause. Concurrency tests observe actual database lock waits for registration, commands, preferences, blocks and dispatch. Recovery repairs forward; it does not reopen old writers or restore stale backups over accepted writes.\n\nVerification:\n\n- Seven PostgreSQL17 SQL property suites pass on fresh 155 schema, including historical activation and migration idempotence. Real concurrent operations cover reactions, duplicate comments, replies/deletion, blocking, mention privacy, catalog revocation and report reopening. The whitespace regression fails before the repair and passes afterward for generated Unicode variants; actual HTTP verifies rejected create/edit preserve body and counts.\n- The encrypted production restore accepted 155 migrations, remains paused, and retains all 30 notifications. Release ancestry/checksum planning, 82 release tests, specification inventory and catalog authority audit pass. The 10,000-comment/2,000-reaction benchmark measured 18.6 ms summary, 6.8 ms roots, 4.9 ms replies and 4.8 ms deep context.\n- Web tests include rendered interaction/permission flows, 19 focused publication-selection cases and real browser journeys across five desktop/mobile configurations with accessibility checks. Backend qualification includes 3,539 examples with zero failures and six existing pending, plus real session/HTTP tests. Current [CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/36525453887) and [release image](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/36525461076) passed on 0a5653dc3; preceding 610773877 CI/image passed. All 37 review findings are addressed. The published image digest was independently matched to CI: `sha256:3e7f5396d9ffa91347578f614ff8356a47bb47e77d721470efff07211fd851d1`. All selected PR jobs pass; the optional Android job is skipped in the default run and qualified by the separate installed journey linked below.\n- [Native PR124](https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/124) merged normally after required checks. Native qualification includes 553 tests, rendered focus/layout regressions, type/lint and Expo startup. The [installed Android journey](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/36520750030) passes reactions, comments, exact reply notification focus, editing, parent deletion and retained replies. Its initial emulator failure was a Pixel Launcher ANR; the fresh-emulator retry passed.\n- Signed Android 22/iOS 29 independently pass receipt hashes, signing identities, production API, runtime and associated-domain checks. Android 22 is saved as a **held, unpublished** Play draft; Alpha 17 remains active. iOS 29 has not been uploaded. The prior iOS installed journey passed; the latest 3ee artifact matches its pinned source and verifies its signature, but its installed journey is **not qualified** because repeated local disk exhaustion prevents reset/reinstallation and even diagnostic-file creation. The owned simulator is shut down. The signed main release and installed Android source trees are identical. Physical VoiceOver/TalkBack and installed HTTPS associations remain unverified.\n\n**Not merged, deployed or activated.** Production remains healthy on its existing backend/ledger 115. GitHub requires fresh independent approval. App Store Connect is signed out, and local iOS verification needs disk space. The release order is documented: pause only automatic Cloudflare production deployments, protected merge commit (no squash/rebase), fresh encrypted backup/rehearsal, immutable schema/backend rollout, association/web/native qualification, guarded activation and production canaries. Preserve Trader and its shared Fly database. No production rollback or activation has been attempted.\n\nArchitecture/invariants: `docs/interactions/implementation.md` and `formal/interactions/README.md`. Migration/recovery: `docs/interactions/rollout.md`. Revision-specific earlier evidence: `docs/interactions/verification-2026-09-29.md`. This PR is not complete against the end-to-end delivery criteria until the remaining qualification and deployment gates pass.\n",
